  "notes": "Fresh-eyes fix worker rotation implemented per Sprint 156 Task 012 spec.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### src/orchestra/debt-manager.ts (+181 LoC)\n- Added MODEL_DOWNGRADE_MAP (Claude/OpenAI/Gemini tier-based downgrade table)\n- Added AGENT_FRESH_EYES_MAP (16 built-in agents paired with complementary fix agents)\n- Exported rotateModelForFix(model): opus→sonnet, sonnet→haiku, gpt-5→gpt-4.1, gemini-2.5-pro→gemini-2.5-flash, etc.\n- Exported rotateAgentForFix(agent): architect→code-reviewer (test spec), bug-fixer→code-reviewer, code-reviewer→bug-fixer, etc. Defaults to 'code-reviewer' for unknown/generic/undefined.\n- Exported applyFreshEyesRotation(originalTask): returns FreshEyesRotationStrategy descriptor\n- Modified handleEvaluation NO_GO branch: fix task now uses rotated model + agent + companion skills (replaces previous copy-model-and-effort behaviour), and writes rotationStrategy field into fix task JSON\n- Also applied rotation to handleCrossDependencies cross-fix tasks for consistency\n- forceModel + forceAgent set on the fix task so V2 routing engine respects the rotation\n- Companion skill 'code-simplifier' added for architect/security-auditor rotations (matches DIRECTIVES \"code-reviewer+bug-fixer\" intent)\n\n### src/orchestra/sprint-spawner.ts (+81 LoC)\n- Added emitRotationMetricIfApplicable() helper that reads rotationStrategy from fix task JSON at spawn-time and emits BRAIN→*:METRIC_EMITTED event + observability metric (name=fix.rotation.applied) — non-blocking, swallows I/O errors\n- Wired into respawnEligibleTasks() spawn loop so each fix-task spawn produces a rotation telemetry event\n- Re-exported rotation helpers (applyFreshEyesRotation, rotateModelForFix, rotateAgentForFix) + FreshEyesRotationStrategy type for external consumers\n\n### tests/orchestra/fresh-eyes-rotation.test.ts (NEW, 388 lines, 36 tests)\n- 9 tests for rotateModelForFix (Claude/OpenAI/Gemini map + safe fallback)\n- 9 tests for rotateAgentForFix (known agents + generic/undefined/null/unknown defaults)\n- 6 tests for applyFreshEyesRotation (strategy shape, companion skills, no-mutate guarantee, terminal model)\n- 6 integration tests for handleEvaluation NO_GO branch:\n  * orig model=opus+agent=architect → fix model=sonnet+agent=code-reviewer (matches Sprint 156 Task 012 test spec)\n  * rotationStrategy field present in fix task JSON\n  * forceModel + forceAgent set for routing override\n  * isPriorityFix/CRITICAL/PENDING preserved\n  * assignedSkills merged (existing + companion)\n  * sonnet+bug-fixer → haiku+code-reviewer\n- 6 tests for sprint-spawner re-export surface + emitRotationMetricIfApplicable safe-fail behaviour\n\n## Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: PASS (no errors)\n- `npx vitest run tests/orchestra/fresh-eyes-rotation.test.ts`: 36/36 PASS\n- `npx vitest run tests/orchestra/debt-manager.test.ts`: 49/49 PASS (no regressions)\n- `npx vitest run tests/orchestra/sprint-spawner.test.ts`: 59/59 PASS (no regressions)\n- Total in-scope tests: 144/144 PASS\n\n## ADR Compliance\n- ADR-008 (Brain Merkezi Import): No new inverse imports — sprint-spawner already imports from worker, and debt-manager does not import sprint-spawner (no cycle introduced).\n- ADR-024 (sprint-controller god split): Both files retain their existing zone — debt-manager owns rotation logic, sprint-spawner owns spawn-time observability.\n- ADR-015 (TaskRouter 6-level routing): Rotation uses forceModel + forceAgent (override layer) so routing decisions respect the rotation deterministically.\n\n## Scope Adherence\nModified ONLY the three files in task spec (src/orchestra/debt-manager.ts, src/orchestra/sprint-spawner.ts, tests/orchestra/fresh-eyes-rotation.test.ts). Task type extension for rotationStrategy was kept out of core/ via JSON payload cast — the field travels with the fix task JSON without modifying the formal Task interface.\n\n## Out-of-Scope Observation (not a regression from my work)\ntests/orchestra/fix-phase-map.test.ts (5 tests) fails on the current branch because Task 003 (Cascade/Unblock Runtime Wire) added applyUnblockToSprint + writeEvent calls inside runFixPhase, but did not extend fix-phase-map.test.ts mocks to cover those calls. This existed before my changes and is outside Task 012's scope. Owner: Task 003.\n\n## Honest Self-Assessment\nBaseline: fix task creation simply copied original task's model + effort, no agent rotation, no rotation_strategy field.\nEnd state: rotation applied at fix task creation (debt-manager.ts), rotation observability at spawn-time (sprint-spawner.ts), 36 dedicated tests covering helpers + integration. Task spec test (model=opus+agent=architect → fix model=sonnet+agent=code-reviewer) explicitly verified. ≥80% of task fully delivered → selfAssessment DONE.",
